cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use Helder, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
title: "Helder: real-time water quality for the Netherlands from open data"
abstract: >-
  Helder is an open data platform that combines Dutch real-time water quality sensors,
  laboratory chemistry, bathing water microbiology, groundwater analyses and drinking water
  quality. It checks every sensor value with QARTOD quality-control tests and physical
  consistency checks, judges values against norms encoded with their legal force, aggregation
  rule, validity period and citation, keeps every revision in a bitemporal lakehouse, and
  publishes results through the OGC SensorThings API, a REST API, CAP alerts and a static
  dashboard. It uses no machine learning.
authors:
  - family-names: Mohammadpour
    given-names: Soheil
repository-code: https://github.com/soheil-mp/helder
url: https://soheil-mp.github.io/helder/
license: MIT
version: 0.0.0
keywords:
